Chapter: LetElseScope

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Regression: a nested let-in inside an else branch must keep its
 binding in scope across the inner 'in'. Historically this could
 mis-scope and read an unallocated slot (EXC=06). Correct results:
 pick 5 7 = 7018, pick (-3) 7 = 7098.

Section: Definitions

  pick : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pick (n) (m) =
    let base = m * 1000
    in let reuse = n - 1
    in if reuse >= 0 then
      let s = reuse + 10 in s + reuse + base
    else let loc = n + 2
    in let s = loc + 100
    in s + loc + base

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (pick 5 7))
    print-line-uni (show (pick (-3) 7))
  end

